# CODEOWNERS — who GitHub automatically asks to review what.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT `*`. A catch-all owner auto-requests the maintainer on every
# pull request, which is precisely the bottleneck GOVERNANCE.md exists to remove:
# one reviewer cannot clear a queue that grows faster than one person reviews.
# Ordinary changes go to the community board and are picked up there.
#
# What IS listed below is the set of paths GOVERNANCE.md § "The merge rule"
# reserves for the maintainer's own security-and-architecture read. Those get an
# automatic review request because forgetting one is expensive.
#
# As triagers are admitted at the weekly community meeting (MAINTAINERS.md),
# their areas are added here so a pull request reaches someone who knows that
# code without anyone having to ask. Adding a line is a pull request like any other.
#
# NOTE: this file REQUESTS reviews. It grants no permission and gates no merge —
# the merge rule is in GOVERNANCE.md.

